#: includes/configs/settings.php:26
msgid "Bar background"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:26
msgid "Fills the whole bar. With the glass effect switched on, this is the colour tinting the blur."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:27
msgid "Bar border"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:27
msgid "The hairline along the very top of the bar, separating it from the page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:28
msgid "Icon colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:28
msgid "The icons on every item except any item using the Prominent style."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:29
msgid "Label colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:29
msgid "The text under, or above, each icon. Items with no label are not affected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:30
msgid "Active colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:30
msgid "Applied to the icon and label of the item whose address exactly matches the page being viewed. Many pages, such as an individual listing, match no item, and nothing is highlighted then. An item using the Prominent style keeps its own icon colour, and only its label changes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:31
msgid "Prominent background"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:31
msgid "The raised circle behind an item set to the Prominent style. Nothing changes if no item uses it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:32
msgid "Prominent icon colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:32
msgid "The icon inside the Prominent circle. Pick something that contrasts strongly with the Prominent background colour."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:33
msgid "Badge background"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:33
msgid "The small counter bubble, shown only on items given a badge and only when the count is above zero."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:34
msgid "Badge text colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:34
msgid "The number inside that bubble."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:62
msgid "Link"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:69
msgid "Icon"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:76
msgid "Label"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:92
msgid "Address for Custom URL"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:99
msgid "Style"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:103
msgid "Default"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:104
msgid "Prominent"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:111
msgid "No badge"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:123
msgid "User Bar"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:124
msgid "Add up to 5 items, shown to everyone who visits your site. If you switch the vendor bar on below, vendors see the Vendor Bar items instead of these. For each item, choose a destination from the first dropdown, then pick an icon and, if you like, the label text shown under it. Drag the handle on a row to move it: the top row becomes the leftmost button, and the items share the width of the bar evenly, so three or four read more comfortably on a narrow phone than five. The Address box is used only when you choose Custom URL, and is ignored for every other choice. The Prominent style lifts an item into a highlighted circle, ideal for one main action. The Badge dropdown picks which unread counter appears on the item, if any. An item is left out of the bar if it has no destination, if you chose Custom URL and left the Address box empty, or if its destination no longer exists, for example a page you have unpublished or one belonging to an extension you have switched off. Icons come from the Font Awesome set HivePress bundles, so if another plugin or your theme replaces or trims that set, check your chosen icons still appear."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:129
msgid "Vendor Bar"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:130
msgid "Add up to 5 items shown to users with a published vendor profile when the vendor bar is enabled. The fields work the same way as the User Bar items above. If none of these items can be shown, for example when the rows are empty or point somewhere that no longer exists, vendors see the User Bar items instead so they are never left without navigation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:136
msgid "Items"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:137
msgid "Add item"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:164
msgid "Action Bar"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:170
msgid "Display"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:171
msgid "The action bar is a fixed strip of buttons pinned to the bottom of the screen, giving your website an app-like feel. It appears based on how wide the browser window is rather than what device someone is using: small screens are up to 767px wide, medium screens are 768px to 1024px, and large screens are anything wider. Tick the sizes you want it on, and if you untick all three it never appears at all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:176
msgid "Small screens"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:177
msgid "Show the action bar on screens up to 767px wide"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:184
msgid "Medium screens"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:185
msgid "Show the action bar on screens 768px to 1024px wide"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:191
msgid "Large screens"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:192
msgid "Show the action bar on screens wider than 1024px"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:193
msgid "Adds the bar on laptops and desktop computers as well. Most sites leave this off, because visitors on a large screen already have your main menu and the bar takes up room at the bottom of every page. It is worth turning on if your site is meant to feel like an app on every screen. The buttons spread out to fill the width, so three or four look better than five."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:199
msgid "Bar height (px)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:200
msgid "How tall the bar is, in pixels. This is a minimum rather than a fixed height: if your labels are large the bar grows to fit them. Between 44 and 120; 56 suits most sites. On iPhones without a home button, extra space is added below this automatically."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:209
msgid "Label position"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:210
msgid "Choose whether item labels sit under the icons or above them. With labels above, an item using the Prominent style keeps its coloured circle but no longer sits raised above the bar."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:214
msgid "Below icons"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:215
msgid "Above icons"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:223
msgid "Label size (px)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:224
msgid "How big the text under each icon is. Between 9 and 16; 11 suits most sites. Larger text makes the bar taller."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:233
msgid "Label weight"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:234
msgid "How thick the label text looks. Medium is a good middle ground; Bold can be hard to read at small sizes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:238
msgid "Normal"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:239
msgid "Medium"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:240
msgid "Semibold"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:241
msgid "Bold"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:258
msgid "Notification badge"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:259
msgid "Allow the notification badge on items"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:260
msgid "Each item has its own Badge dropdown. Account activity (HivePress) shows HivePress's own combined unread count, the same number as the one beside your name in the site header, which the Messages, Bookings and Marketplace extensions add to. With none of those three installed it stays at zero. Unread messages counts messages only, and appears in the dropdown whenever the Messages extension is active. It stays at zero unless \"Store messages in the database\" is ticked under HivePress, Settings, Messages, because with that box unticked messages are emailed rather than stored, so there is nothing to count. Unread notifications counts only unread notifications from Notifications for HivePress, and appears in the dropdown only when that plugin is active. Untick this box to hide every badge at once."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:267
msgid "Vendor bar"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:268
msgid "Show different items to vendors"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:269
msgid "If enabled, users with a published vendor profile see the Vendor Bar items instead of the User Bar items. Tick to reveal the Vendor Bar section below."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:275
msgid "Room for the home bar"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:276
msgid "Leave space below the bar on iPhones without a home button"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:277
msgid "On iPhones without a home button there is a thin bar at the very bottom of the screen that can overlap your buttons. Ticking this asks the browser to report how much room to leave, and the action bar then sits above it. It is safe to leave ticked whatever your theme does, and it has no effect on other phones."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:283
msgid "Glass effect"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:284
msgid "Blur the page showing through the bar"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:285
msgid "Makes the bar semi-transparent and blurs whatever scrolls behind it, the frosted look used by phone apps. Pick a light bar colour for a light site and a dark one for a dark site, then check that your icons and labels are still easy to read against your busiest page. Older browsers that cannot blur keep the solid bar instead, and visitors who have asked their device to reduce transparency also see the solid bar."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:291
msgid "Glass opacity (%)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:292
msgid "How solid the bar colour stays over the blur. Lower shows more of the page, higher keeps labels easier to read. Between 10 and 100; 72 suits most sites, and at 100 the bar is solid so the effect no longer shows."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:302
msgid "Glass blur (px)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:303
msgid "How strongly the page behind the bar is blurred. Between 0 and 40; 20 gives the frosted look. At 0 the page stays sharp behind the tint, though colours showing through still look slightly richer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:313
msgid "Glass top edge"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:314
msgid "Add a soft light along the top edge"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:315
msgid "Draws a faint white highlight across the very top of the bar, which is what makes frosted glass read as glass rather than as a flat tint. It shows up best on a dark or mid-toned bar; on a near-white bar it will not be visible either way."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:325
msgid "Visibility"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:326
msgid "Choose where the action bar stays hidden, for example pages that need the visitor's full attention, or the steps where someone is paying."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:331
msgid "Hide on pages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:332
msgid "The bar is hidden on the pages you pick here. This list covers WordPress pages only, so it cannot be used to hide the bar on listings, vendor profiles or search results."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:341
msgid "Checkout pages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:342
msgid "Hide the action bar on the WooCommerce cart and checkout pages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:343
msgid "This only has an effect if WooCommerce is installed. Payment or booking pages provided by other extensions are not covered, so hide those with Hide on pages above."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:352
msgid "Colours"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:353
msgid "Customise the action bar colours. Use the colour wheel, or type a hex code such as #f5f5f5. Short codes like #fff are expanded for you, and the # is added if you leave it off. Clear a field and save to put that colour back to its default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:369
msgid "Removing the Plugin"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:370
msgid "Your bar items and settings are kept if you delete this plugin, so you can reinstall it and carry on where you left off. WordPress shows its own warning on the delete screen saying the data goes too, but that warning is the same for every plugin and does not apply here unless you tick the box below. Switching the plugin off never removes anything."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:375
msgid "Delete all data"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:376
msgid "Delete everything when this plugin is deleted"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:377
msgid "Leave this unticked unless you are certain. With it ticked, deleting the plugin also removes every item you have added to the User Bar and the Vendor Bar, your colours, and every other setting on this page. WordPress will still ask you to confirm the deletion itself, but that confirmation says nothing about this box, so the removal happens with no second chance. It cannot be undone, so write down anything you want to keep first. Deleting the plugin with this unticked keeps all of it."
msgstr ""

